zAYab0QIgwCzSupUlP16rZ7G/view?fbclid=IwAR346jgS_kx0e1hy0-orffAHM1cq7JuHmX4wgQYDZzLRBAPi381KIRJMfvw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T17:18:18-07:00","id":1464290,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm going to have to consult around with some Storyteller Vault veterans about how to make my book. I made an RPG like 20 years ago but don't know anything about how to do it now in terms of layout, art, and so one.<br /> <br /> However, I am excited about doing a Chronicle in Gary to follow up Let the Streets Run Red.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T00:38:25-07:00","id":1464326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1464287#post1464287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, here's a sample: I haven't bought any since I have my own Sabbat rules so cavet emptor:<br /> <br /> GUIDE TO THE SABBAT 5th Edition: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=newest_community&amp;filters=45622_45624_45645\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...22_45624_45645</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So here's my informal review of Guide to the Sabbat (V5) by Jay Haller et al.<br /> <br /> In short: it's pretty good. The editor needs to fix some typos (a glaring one is the misspelling of Kiasyd throughout the book) and formatting issues (there are neither indents nor line spacing between paragraphs, for example) and they need to read the style guide for consistency, but these are all issues endemic to self- and indie-published works (including those on STV). Especially since this is cheap or free (PWYW), I think we can overlook those things.<br /> <br /> Other than these superficial issues, the mechanics themselves look solid and the design is great. I really like how they approach Paths, and the Vaulderie rules are simple and straightforward. The Loresheets and Disciplines add a lot of nuance and flavour. <br /> <br /> Overall, I would give this a 3.5/5. It would get 4/5 if they fixed the typos, paragraph spacing and style issues, and 5/5 if they gave more info in the initial chapters on the history and structure of the Sabbat (though there's a lot buried in the Loresheets, I must admit).<br /> <br /> Honestly, this one is definitely worth picking up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 10-18-2021, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T02:08:20-07:00","id":1464335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1464326#post1464326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's pretty good. The editor needs to fix some typos (a glaring one is the misspelling of Kiasyd throughout the book) and formatting issues (there are neither indents nor line spacing between paragraphs, for example) and they need to read the style guide for consistency, but these are all issues endemic to self- and indie-published and STV works. Especially since this is cheap, I think we can overlook those issues.<br /> <br /> Other than these superficial issues, the mechanics themselves look solid and the design is great. I really like how they approach Paths, and the Vaulderie rules are simple and straightforward. The Loresheets and Disciplines add a lot of nuance and flavour.<br /> <br /> Overall, I would give this a 3.5/5. It would get 4/5 if they fixed the typos, paragraph spacing and style issues, and 5/5 if they gave more info in the initial chapters on the history and structure of the Sabbat (though there's a lot buried in the Loresheets, I must admit).<br /> <br /> Honestly, this one is definitely worth picking up!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of the three there, this one seems the best especially as its PWYW for a similar amount of info that the other two have,<br /> <br /> LHROOH is cheap enough that it would be worth picking up in unison with it.<br /> <br /> TSOC I'm not so sure its worth $20 after seeing the author throw a tantrum on FB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T05:05:36-07:00","id":1464355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1464335#post1464335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Of the three there, this one seems the best especially as its PWYW for a similar amount of info that the other two have,<br /> <br /> LHROOH is cheap enough that it would be worth picking up in unison with it.<br /> <br /> TSOC I'm not so sure its worth $20 after seeing the author throw a tantrum on FB.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the new version of The Long Road Out of Hell different to the free one most of us already have? I think V5 GttS does Paths better, and simpler, though LRooH is neat if you like Touchstones. GttS uses your packmates as Touchstones, which is super simple and quite appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T10:26:32-07:00","id":1464389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1464355#post1464355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is the new version of The Long Road Out of Hell different to the free one most of us already have? I think V5 GttS does Paths better, and simpler, though LRooH is neat if you like Touchstones. GttS uses your packmates as Touchstones, which is super simple and quite appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Long Road Out of Hell has the Beast Marks system, though, and I adore Beast Marks. Just an amazing idea for personalizing the alien nature of your character. I also love the idea of, for example, considering the graveyard where you got your creation rites to be your Touchstone. I have this as two of my characters, and it has been lots of fun roleplaying the various complications of needing to visit and maintain this graveyard.<br /> <br /> &quot;Simpler&quot; isn't an automatic plus to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 10-18-2021, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T12:58:44-07:00","id":1464408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1464389#post1464389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Long Road Out of Hell has the Beast Marks system, though, and I adore Beast Marks. Just an amazing idea for personalizing the alien nature of your character. I also love the idea of, for example, considering the graveyard where you got your creation rites to be your Touchstone. I have this as two of my characters, and it has been lots of fun roleplaying the various complications of needing to visit and maintain this graveyard.<br /> <br /> &quot;Simpler&quot; isn't an automatic plus to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast Marks are cool, but the Paths are more faithful in V5 GttS. So YMMV.<br /> <br /> You could always use the LRooH Touchstones and everything else from V5 GttS (such as the Loresheets and Disciplines).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T19:32:27-07:00","id":1464677,"title":"","content":"The only thing I didn't liked about the Vaulderie rules on the sample (I didn't got the book yet as I do want to consider how much I'll pay) was they completely overtake previous Convictions/Touchstones. I like this as an option, not as unavoidable, as it makes the Vaulderie alone to be the single thing that eliminates almost every tie to humans the character had before. I would put it as optionally adding just one Conviction and the whole Pack as Touchstone for this Conviction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T19:40:04-07:00","id":1464679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374104/The-Sword-of-Caine-A-V5-Guide-to-the-Sabbat\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/374104.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374104/The-Sword-of-Caine-A-V5-Guide-to-the-Sabbat\" target=\"_blank\"> The Sword of Caine: A V5 Guide to the Sabbat - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374104/The-Sword-of-Caine-A-V5-Guide-to-the-Sabbat\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374104/The-Sword-of-Caine-A-V5-Guide-to-the-Sabbat </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Sword of Caine: A V5 Guide to the Sabbat - The Gehenna War Calls The Sword of Caine has often been viewed by the Camarilla as monstrous beasts that live only to di </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Here's another one that's come out.<br /> <br /> Cool beanz.<br /> <br /> We'll have a competition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T23:34:29-07:00","id":1464703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1464679#post1464679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374104/The-Sword-of-Caine-A-V5-Guide-to-the-Sabbat\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...-to-the-Sabbat</a><br /> <br /> Here's another one that's come out.<br /> <br /> Cool beanz.<br /> <br /> We'll have a competition.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I've now read The Sword of Caine: A V5 Guide to the Sabbat too.<br /> <br /> This one has all the background material that V5 GttS doesn't, and has fewer typos, but they do consistently get some things wrong (like misspelling Melinda Galbraith's name).<br /> <br /> Anyway, design-wise, this is a gorgeous book. It has lots of crunch, and presents rules for all the Sabbat ritae and the Paths. I don't like the rules for Paths quite as much (you only pick one Ethic, for example) but it seems relatively straightforward.<br /> <br /> The Loresheets and Disciplines don't feel as strong as in V5 GttS, and I was surprised to see Vicissitude and Valeren return despite these Disciplines being covered in other V5 books, and was also surprised that they then didn't do the same with Obtenebretion (which needed it more).<br /> <br /> This book fits with the V5 metaplot, though, which is a strong selling point if you like V5 but want to keep the Sabbat, but of course the Sabbat is still very different if you're more into the Revised/V20 presentation (it's described as having experienced the Reformation).<br /> <br /> You can also find all the Bloodlines and antitribu here, which is very welcome. No fishing around in multiple books for this one. There are new Predator Types to go with it.<br /> <br /> I'd give it 4/5. It's about on a par with V5 GttS but with better production values.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 10-21-2021, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T03:13:29-07:00","id":1464713,"title":"","content":"Having read all three GttS is definitely the one thats come out on top for me.<br /> <br /> Admittedly SoC lost points when the author went ballistic in the Storytellers Vault Facebook Group over an imagined slight, but even without that GttS was still heads and shoulders above the other two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T03:16:37-07:00","id":1464714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1464290#post1464290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm going to have to consult around with some Storyteller Vault veterans about how to make my book. I made an RPG like 20 years ago but don't know anything about how to do it now in terms of layout, art, and so one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of helpful folks in the STV Discord if your interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T04:03:35-07:00","id":1464715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1464714#post1464714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lots of helpful folks in the STV Discord if your interested.</div> </div> </div> </div>Already getting some awesome help. This is such a wonderful community.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T04:19:14-07:00","id":1464719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1464713#post1464713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having read all three GttS is definitely the one thats come out on top for me.<br /> <br /> Admittedly SoC lost points when the author went ballistic in the Storytellers Vault Facebook Group over an imagined slight, but even without that GttS was still heads and shoulders above the other two.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's fair. I gave this 4/5 mainly for production and completeness, but if GttS could be touched up and edited properly, that one inches out on SoC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1464714#post1464714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lots of helpful folks in the STV Discord if your interested.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take the link, if you have it. I want to do a Grognard's Guide which is basically an evolution of the V20 setting with some smoother mechanics (I'm quite pleased with the changes I've made to Morality and Hunger that mean 'you are what you do', and so you have to practice what you preach to retain high levels of control and composure). I've been tentatively calling this V30, and it's quite detailed already, so I need to pull everything together and design it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T20:44:43-07:00","id":1464821,"title":"","content":"[<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1464719#post1464719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's fair. I gave this 4/5 mainly for production and completeness, but if GttS could be touched up and edited properly, that one inches out on SoC.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'll take the link, if you have it. I want to do a Grognard's Guide which is basically an evolution of the V20 setting with some smoother mechanics (I'm quite pleased with the changes I've made to Morality and Hunger that mean 'you are what you do', and so you have to practice what you preach to retain high levels of control and composure). I've been tentatively calling this V30, and it's quite detailed already, so I need to pull everything together and design it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just make sure to watch the scope of your writing, as you can't create a brand new core rule book or 'edition' of a game for the ST Vault or something that invalidates the need for a published, official core rule book. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller's Vault Content Questions</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b><b>Can I create standalone core rulebooks or new editions?</b></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">No. Storytellers Vault content should be supplemental to official core books and game lines. You cannot replace the need for an official core rulebook with your Storytellers Vault supplement. This includes historical books and settings.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">You cannot publish new editions of core rulebooks or without authorization.<br /> </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T00:16:56-07:00","id":1464831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1464821#post1464821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[<br /> <br /> <br /> Just make sure to watch the scope of your writing, as you can't create a brand new core rule book or 'edition' of a game for the ST Vault or something that invalidates the need for a published, official core rule book. <br /> <br /> [/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know. It's a fine balance. To keep things as supplemental, it's more a conversion and toolkit, so I have a table for how to convert V20 and V5 difficulties, for example, and I don't repeat all the fluff. Where things remain unchanged, I refer to V20 or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T00:30:20-07:00","id":1464833,"title":"","content":"16K done on my manuscript. I'm really inspired by the fact they're doing these things now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T20:14:26-08:00","id":1467408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1464326#post1464326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So here's my informal review of Guide to the Sabbat (V5) by Jay Haller et al.<br /> <br /> In short: it's pretty good. The editor needs to fix some typos (a glaring one is the misspelling of Kiasyd throughout the book) and formatting issues (there are neither indents nor line spacing between paragraphs, for example) and they need to read the style guide for consistency, but these are all issues endemic to self- and indie-published works (including those on STV). Especially since this is cheap or free (PWYW), I think we can overlook those things.<br /> <br /> Other than these superficial issues, the mechanics themselves look solid and the design is great. I really like how they approach Paths, and the Vaulderie rules are simple and straightforward. The Loresheets and Disciplines add a lot of nuance and flavour.<br /> <br /> Overall, I would give this a 3.5/5. It would get 4/5 if they fixed the typos, paragraph spacing and style issues, and 5/5 if they gave more info in the initial chapters on the history and structure of the Sabbat (though there's a lot buried in the Loresheets, I must admit).<br /> <br /> Honestly, this one is definitely worth picking up!</div> </div> </div> </div>Jay here, really glad you enjoyed the book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Very happy to hear you like the mechanics we came up with especially. Certainly took plenty of tinkering, the Path system we present was our 4th take or so. On the whole, our intent was to try and create simple rules hewing as close toV5's design principles as possible, whilst doing justice to the Sabbat we all know and love. We wanted to provide Storytellers and Players with the mechanics to let them portray any interpretation of the Sabbat they chose, not impose our preferred version.<br /> <br /> To address your points for improvement if I may:<br /> <b>Formatting - </b>We are currently in the process of collecting details for an update (mistakes, things people would like clarified, etc). If I might be so bold we threw together a little feedback &amp; errata form. We're doing our best to catch all the mistakes, but extra eyes always help and we're very keen to get the community's input. <a href=\"https://forms.gle/cmWQfeyecJnjuDVK8\" target=\"_blank\">https://forms.gle/cmWQfeyecJnjuDVK8</a><br /> <br /> <b>History &amp; Structure -</b> We had drafts that included a lot of that sort of information. Breakdowns of ranks (including sub-sects), lexicon, punishment within the sect even. We were worried it would hew too close to official content though and were unsure about copyright limmitations. (This was our first STV project so we didn't want to push our luck!)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1464677#post1464677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I didn't liked about the Vaulderie rules on the sample (I didn't got the book yet as I do want to consider how much I'll pay) was they completely overtake previous Convictions/Touchstones. I like this as an option, not as unavoidable, as it makes the Vaulderie alone to be the single thing that eliminates almost every tie to humans the character had before. I would put it as optionally adding just one Conviction and the whole Pack as Touchstone for this Conviction.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thinking with the vaulderie design was that it severs your ties to others in a supernatural way, replacing them with blood-enduced loyalty. Thus, a Sabbat under the vaulderie doesn't retain mortal touchstones, but they might still care about mortals that once functioned as such. (Just not to the extent that it allows them to stave off damage to their morality/soul/rational self, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":25061,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","user":"Karos","date":".  HTML formatting error. 11-10-2021, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T00:04:16-08:00","id":1467417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1467408#post1467408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Jay here, really glad you enjoyed the book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Very happy to hear you like the mechanics we came up with especially. Certainly took plenty of tinkering, the Path system we present was our 4th take or so. On the whole, our intent was to try and create simple rules hewing as close toV5's design principles as possible, whilst doing justice to the Sabbat we all know and love. We wanted to provide Storytellers and Players with the mechanics to let them portray any interpretation of the Sabbat they chose, not impose our preferred version.<br /> <br /> To address your points for improvement if I may:<br /> <b>Formatting - </b>We are currently in the process of collecting details for an update (mistakes, things people would like clarified, etc). If I might be so bold we threw together a little feedback &amp; errata form. We're doing our best to catch all the mistakes, but extra eyes always help and we're very keen to get the community's input. <a href=\"https://forms.gle/cmWQfeyecJnjuDVK8\" target=\"_blank\">https://forms.gle/cmWQfeyecJnjuDVK8</a><br /> <br /> <b>History &amp; Structure -</b> We had drafts that included a lot of that sort of information. Breakdowns of ranks (including sub-sects), lexicon, punishment within the sect even. We were worried it would hew too close to official content though and were unsure about copyright limmitations. (This was our first STV project so we didn't want to push our luck!)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My thinking with the vaulderie design was that it severs your ties to others in a supernatural way, replacing them with blood-enduced loyalty. Thus, a Sabbat under the vaulderie doesn't retain mortal touchstones, but they might still care about mortals that once functioned as such. (Just not to the extent that it allows them to stave off damage to their morality/soul/rational self, etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of background info, you should be fine there. The STV rules stipulate you can't do a new edition and can't only publish existing material, but you can reuse existing material if it's presented with significantly new material.<br /> <br /> So I would say that including sect history and fluff is perfectly acceptable, so long as it's not a copy and paste of Revised GttS and adds something new. The mechanics themselves add a lot of new stuff, so I think the book would go far enough to meet the test for originality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T05:16:24-08:00","id":1467430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1467408#post1467408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thinking with the vaulderie design was that it severs your ties to others in a supernatural way, replacing them with blood-enduced loyalty. Thus, a Sabbat under the vaulderie doesn't retain mortal touchstones, but they might still care about mortals that once functioned as such. (Just not to the extent that it allows them to stave off damage to their morality/soul/rational self, etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with the complete overhaul is that it have precisely the problem of shutting down options.<br /> <br /> Convictions and Touchstones are the main touch of individuality for the character in the new Humanity system (something the old system didn't even had), and one of the interesting themes they bring is the lingering of old ties and beliefs, and how they can add to or conflict with your life as a vampire.<br /> <br /> Adding one Conviction and the Pack as its Touchstone makes for a good benefit for the Vaulderie, as you gain a new Conviction and at the same time keep the theme. At character creation the player have then a choice to keep making the other Convictions tied either to the mortal life or the Vaulderie. Overhauling removes one of those options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T17:36:00-08:00","id":1467618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1467417#post1467417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In terms of background info, you should be fine there. The STV rules stipulate you can't do a new edition and can't only publish existing material, but you can reuse existing material if it's presented with significantly new material.<br /> <br /> So I would say that including sect history and fluff is perfectly acceptable, so long as it's not a copy and paste of Revised GttS and adds something new. The mechanics themselves add a lot of new stuff, so I think the book would go far enough to meet the test for originality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We got some generally mixed messages on that one I found, at least asking around in the STV discord. Of course, they can't say explicitly X would be fine, Y would not. But I was generally under the impression, that even taking bits of text for common mechanics should be avoided. (E.g. we changed the rationales on the hierarchy of sins after being advised that would be safer than using the V20 one's verbatim.)<br /> <br /> That said, we've certainly got a better handle on things now after our first release, so I'm confident in saying there'll be more flavour-text/lore included in our next few releases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1467430#post1467430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with the complete overhaul is that it have precisely the problem of shutting down options.<br /> <br /> Convictions and Touchstones are the main touch of individuality for the character in the new Humanity system (something the old system didn't even had), and one of the interesting themes they bring is the lingering of old ties and beliefs, and how they can add to or conflict with your life as a vampire.<br /> <br /> Adding one Conviction and the Pack as its Touchstone makes for a good benefit for the Vaulderie, as you gain a new Conviction and at the same time keep the theme. At character creation the player have then a choice to keep making the other Convictions tied either to the mortal life or the Vaulderie. Overhauling removes one of those options.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that argument, obviously what you do in your home game is up to you. I can certainly see an interesting story where those two sets of ties conflict and you have to address that conflict as a character.<br /> <br /> My intent in part, however, was to emphasise that the Vaulderie isn't all benefit, it has major drawbacks for those who partake. Chiefly that it engenders false loyalty and camaraderie with people you might not know or otherwise care about.<br /> <br /> You find yourself loving your murders, your abusers, the psychopath in your pack who takes to Sabbat unlife, etc. Not because of any true rational reason, but because the twisted power of the blood forces you to. All the while, your mortal ties are shattered, because in comparison your mortal ties just don't have the same magical strength to them. (This helps parallel indoctrination techniques and tactics used in real-life cults, how they cut you off from loved ones, try and re-direct those feeling internally, etc.)<br /> <br /> It restricts options as a player essentially, to try and reflect the fact that the Sabbat are using rituals and manipulation to restrict your options and dependencies as a character. They want you to depend on no one except your fellow Sabbat, and so that's what the ritae does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T22:25:25-08:00","id":1467642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1467618#post1467618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My intent in part, however, was to emphasise that the Vaulderie isn't all benefit, it has major drawbacks for those who partake. Chiefly that it engenders false loyalty and camaraderie with people you might not know or otherwise care about.<br /> <br /> You find yourself loving your murders, your abusers, the psychopath in your pack who takes to Sabbat unlife, etc. Not because of any true rational reason, but because the twisted power of the blood forces you to. All the while, your mortal ties are shattered, because in comparison your mortal ties just don't have the same magical strength to them. (This helps parallel indoctrination techniques and tactics used in real-life cults, how they cut you off from loved ones, try and re-direct those feeling internally, etc.)<br /> <br /> It restricts options as a player essentially, to try and reflect the fact that the Sabbat are using rituals and manipulation to restrict your options and dependencies as a character. They want you to depend on no one except your fellow Sabbat, and so that's what the ritae does.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually a very interesting rationale, you can count me convinced. Although I would add to the book a sidebox with this exact explanation, almost verbatim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T05:30:39-08:00","id":1467671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1467642#post1467642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is actually a very interesting rationale, you can count me convinced. Although I would add to the book a sidebox with this exact explanation, almost verbatim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something I can look at in our errata pass. Though I daren't make promises without consulting our layout artist first! Changing a few words is no bother, adding large paragraphs sadly can have quite the knock-on effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T06:05:06-08:00","id":1467674,"title":"","content":"The thing is if you go too hard on the power and importance of the Vaulderie, you limit playability. In my opinion, the Vaulderie should be just powerful enough to prevent casual murder among Sabbat. Past that you get problems in story-engine terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T11:34:03-08:00","id":1467700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1467671#post1467671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I daren't make promises without consulting our layout artist first!</div> </div> </div> </div>They'll probably want to kill us, as I know first hand how hard this work is. Hence why I said <i>I would do</i>, not that it should be done. Actually getting to it is far easier to say than to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T14:02:31-08:00","id":1467721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1467674#post1467674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is if you go too hard on the power and importance of the Vaulderie, you limit playability. In my opinion, the Vaulderie should be just powerful enough to prevent casual murder among Sabbat. Past that you get problems in story-engine terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we still have enough flexibility in the system for it not to restrict play excessively. Obviously, I can only speak from the playtesting we did and the feedback I've been given by those who've played using our rules. But from those, it hasn't proven too restrictive to my knowledge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1467700#post1467700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'll probably want to kill us, as I know first hand how hard this work is. Hence why I said <i>I would do</i>, not that it should be done. Actually getting to it is far easier to say than to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, you raise a valid point though, and I did address that sort of design intent elsewhere in the book. In an ideal world, I'd look to add it, I just wanted to clarify in case anyone gets a copy of the update and wonders why it's not there, should it prove impractical to include.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T21:59:40-08:00","id":1470007,"title":"","content":"My first official unofficial <i>Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition</i> supplement. Special thanks to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1208_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1208\" data-vbnamecard=\"1208\">Grumpy RPG Reviews</a> <br /> <br /> THE MURDER OF MODIUS<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/380138/The-Murder-of-Modius\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/2570/380138.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/380138/The-Murder-of-Modius\" target=\"_blank\"> The Murder of Modius - Phipps Studios | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/380138/The-Murder-of-Modius\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/380138/The-Murder-of-Modius </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Murder of Modius - \"Modius is dead and the whole city of Gary is a suspect!\"The Murder of Modius is a Chronicle for Vampire: The Masquerade </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Su