ted":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-06T23:14:43-08:00","id":1474107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474102#post1474102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, this strongly feels like someone rejected their pitch for Playable Sabbat info.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But why? *insert Ryan Reynolds gif meme<br /> <br /> -Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T00:21:30-08:00","id":1474111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474107#post1474107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But why? *insert Ryan Reynolds gif meme<br /> <br /> -Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the pure conjecture answer that the reason that Paradox Entertainment has such a mad on/hatred for the idea of playable Sabbat is a straight line dating back to the controveries of 5th Edition's release.<br /> <br /> They've had to deal with the following:<br /> <br /> * The Nazi Brujah one-line mention as a player character option getting a massive storm of controversy<br /> * The pedophile Ventrue (which wasn't even a pedophile, they just fed on children) in the sample adventure.<br /> * The entire international media shitstorm regarding the vampires in Chechnya.<br /> <br /> My assumption is that all of the bad optics from these events convinced Paradox that doing the Sabbat as player characters, you know, a group of terrorist serial killer religious fanatics <i>even when they're heroes</i> would be something that would bring down even more holy hell of controversy.<br /> <br /> This is why they have an absolutely 100% no holds barred &quot;there will never be playable Sabbat&quot; and we didn't get a Sabbat book until now: terror of controversy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T06:42:12-08:00","id":1474123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474111#post1474111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why they have an absolutely 100% no holds barred &quot;there will never be playable Sabbat&quot; and we didn't get a Sabbat book until now: terror of controversy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vampire community is one of the most toxic you can deal with, with people arguing on basically everything. I swear to Caine I saw a discussion about the correct way vampire should salute one another in larps.<br /> <br /> In this mess, it's hard to sell something to people who are so easily displeased. V5 turned the edition war into a three-front conflict, and the unplayable sabbat was the coup de grace.<br /> <br /> Now, why sell something canonical that will displease at least half your customers, when you can save money by having everyone write what they want, earning a percentage of sales?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T06:49:26-08:00","id":1474124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Riccardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474123#post1474123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The vampire community is one of the most toxic you can deal with, with people arguing on basically everything. I swear to Caine I saw a discussion about the correct way vampire should salute one another in larps.<br /> <br /> In this mess, it's hard to sell something to people who are so easily displeased. V5 turned the edition war into a three-front conflict, and the unplayable sabbat was the coup de grace.<br /> <br /> Now, why sell something canonical that will displease at least half your customers, when you can save money by having everyone write what they want, earning a percentage of sales?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://goconstellation.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/This-is-Why-We-cant-Have-Nice-Things.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I admit I'm only guessing on this part but I do believe that it explains why Paradox is taking such a militant stance against what was previously one of the three pillars of Vampire: The Masquerade. V5 was plagued with controversy and personal attacks when they were trying to revive the brand so an attempt to just avoid all that seems like the most likely reason. I don't think it was an artistic decision but just something to head off another potential massive problem.<br /> <br /> Ironically, I think they would have probably gotten no flak from the &quot;hardcore&quot; fans of V:TM because everyone already KNOWS what the Sabbat is there but were probably more terrified of the people who weren't fans of the Sabbat from the outside making a stink about it.<br /> <br /> Still, the controversy will continue in other places with the Hunter: The Reckoning release [no Imbued] and the &quot;Dead Gaia&quot; Werewolf: The Apocalypse. I think they just didn't feel the Sabbat was a fight they could win.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T08:25:43-08:00","id":1474126,"title":"","content":"I have some doubts. There are still many details in the books that don't quite add up to this strategy, and overall the stance taken wirth the Sabbat is kind of worse from this POV, as discussed in another thread and demonstrated by how far we got in that discussion.<br /> <br /> This is a reasonable thesis if we assume they're not the smartest lot about it, but I do suspect they have other (maybe even simpler) reasons. One possibility is that they just side with players that don't like the Sabbat and have a vision for the game that doesn't include it. Remember that as they can let people publish those in the Vault without assuming liability, they can also just ignore those books and contradict them as non-canon when they please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T09:24:21-08:00","id":1474128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474111#post1474111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have the pure conjecture answer that the reason that Paradox Entertainment has such a mad on/hatred for the idea of playable Sabbat is a straight line dating back to the controveries of 5th Edition's release.<br /> <br /> They've had to deal with the following:<br /> <br /> * The Nazi Brujah one-line mention as a player character option getting a massive storm of controversy<br /> * The pedophile Ventrue (which wasn't even a pedophile, they just fed on children) in the sample adventure.<br /> * The entire international media shitstorm regarding the vampires in Chechnya.<br /> <br /> My assumption is that all of the bad optics from these events convinced Paradox that doing the Sabbat as player characters, you know, a group of terrorist serial killer religious fanatics <i>even when they're heroes</i> would be something that would bring down even more holy hell of controversy.<br /> <br /> This is why they have an absolutely 100% no holds barred &quot;there will never be playable Sabbat&quot; and we didn't get a Sabbat book until now: terror of controversy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's no coincidence that we got word of the official 'Antagonists Only' Sabbat book, shortly followed by V5 content being allowed on the STV. Putting on my conspiracy-theorist hat, it's not beyond the pale to suggest they wanted to cash in on playable Sabbat, without the risks of such a project in the current climate. Therefore, they made it so we the community could write the content, then publish it through their licensed homebrew system.<br /> <br /> - No development overheads for them.<br /> - No direct backlash or risk involved for the company.<br /> - The ability to disavow any heinous products and make a show of doing so.<br /> - All whilst taking 50% of the profits of anything that secured community support.<br /> <br /> Not that that's a bad thing, it's meant:<br /> - Profit for the community (be a bit of a hypocrite if I had an issue with self-published Sabbat!)<br /> - A variety of takes on the Sabbat in V5 to suit various parts of the community<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Long Road out of Hell<br /> The Sword of Caine<br /> Black Hand: Playing the Sabbat<br /> Guide to the Sabbat</div> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T09:35:37-08:00","id":1474129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474111#post1474111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have the pure conjecture answer that the reason that Paradox Entertainment has such a mad on/hatred for the idea of playable Sabbat is a straight line dating back to the controveries of 5th Edition's release.<br /> <br /> They've had to deal with the following:<br /> <br /> * The Nazi Brujah one-line mention as a player character option getting a massive storm of controversy<br /> * The pedophile Ventrue (which wasn't even a pedophile, they just fed on children) in the sample adventure.<br /> * The entire international media shitstorm regarding the vampires in Chechnya.<br /> <br /> My assumption is that all of the bad optics from these events convinced Paradox that doing the Sabbat as player characters, you know, a group of terrorist serial killer religious fanatics <i>even when they're heroes</i> would be something that would bring down even more holy hell of controversy.<br /> <br /> This is why they have an absolutely 100% no holds barred &quot;there will never be playable Sabbat&quot; and we didn't get a Sabbat book until now: terror of controversy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's literally not at all related to what they said as to why Sabbat wasn't written to be playable. I hate that the fandom is on this'[thing does not exist now] because it's too dark and awful!' train. There's plenty of awful shit in the game that hasn't been cut or neutered or whatever, including one of your examples (the neo-nazi line is still in the core book and was never removed). From the Discord (since I can't directly quote Achilli's interviews).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>outstar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s the official statement on the direction of World of Darkness franchise?<br /> <br /> We gave an interview to VentureBeat about a year ago that goes in detail into that subject, and I would say it didn\u2019t age badly at all! Please check it out here: <a href=\"https://venturebeat.com/2020/08/02/for-world-of-darkness-the-future-of-tabletop-rpgs-is-increasingly-digital/\" target=\"_blank\">https://venturebeat.com/2020/08/02/f...ingly-digital/</a><br /> <br /> The keywords are \u201cmedia-agnostic\u201d and \u201ctransmedia\u201d. Since then, we\u2019ve announced our Hollywood-adjacent partnership and plans of bringing WoD to small and big screens, which also explains it further. Our stories need to work at the TTRPG table just like they need to work in a video game, comic book, actual play, immersive experience or on the silver screen - and our approach to IP development treats this as a baseline. TTRPG corebooks become guides for our partners on how to work with our IPs, and when we write these materials, we keep this firmly in mind.<br /> <br /> To give a live example - explanations on how antagonists in V5 Sabbat behave in detail, what sounds or gestures they would make - this is super helpful for storytellers at the tables, but also it would help TV writers nail this down in a script, or video game designers develop them well for in-game worlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's literally about making things more accessible and easier to use in trans-media productions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474128#post1474128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's no coincidence that we got word of the official 'Antagonists Only' Sabbat book, shortly followed by V5 content being allowed on the STV. Putting on my conspiracy-theorist hat, it's not beyond the pale to suggest they wanted to cash in on playable Sabbat, without the risks of such a project in the current climate. Therefore, they made it so we the community could write the content, then publish it through their licensed homebrew system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's pretty tinfoil hat. Even if it were some case of Paradox saying 'hey we'll get money for this with no overhead' it's... the Storyteller's Vault. They'll make a couple thousand bucks since they only get 50% of the sale rates, it's not like this is something in store with thousands and thousands of potential sales from being in stores.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 02-07-2022, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T09:39:34-08:00","id":1474130,"title":"","content":"Double post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T09:53:57-08:00","id":1474132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474129#post1474129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's pretty tinfoil hat. Even if it were some case of Paradox saying 'hey we'll get money for this with no overhead' it's... the Storyteller's Vault. They'll make a couple thousand bucks since they only get 50% of the sale rates, it's not like this is something in store with thousands and thousands of potential sales from being in stores.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh definitely, that's me being as cynical as I could possibly be, though it'd be less of a profit thing. More of serving the community's interest with no risk of backlash; whilst happening to make a little on the side (rather than nothing at all). Homebrew Sabbat rules were going to be written for V5 one way or another, this way they make some money from it and have some control over what's permitted to be associated with their brand.<br /> <br /> Not that we'd ever know of course and why they've done things the way they have is utterly irrelevant at the end of the day. 'Tis what it is, we can only make the best of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T09:57:12-08:00","id":1474133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474129#post1474129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's literally about making things more accessible and easier to use in trans-media productions.</div> </div> </div> </div>They clearly want their books to inform people making video games, board games, comics, films etc. but in what way is that incompatible with making the Sabbat playable at the table? The video games that we already have mostly follow the written setting, but structure stories and the capabilities of characters according to their own requirements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T11:46:04-08:00","id":1474139,"title":"","content":"It's that, plus what Achilli has said in many interviews that have been posted on here a bunch: Sabbat is antithetical to the 'core gameplay' of V5, which is also why they weren't written playable (which I didn't figure bore repeating, but here we are).<br /> <br /> Both, together, pretty much paint the picture: the core vampires are supposed to focus on Humanity, as well as be what could be considered the 'protagonists,' and from an external standpoint, not having them written as playable means you don't have the baseline possibly coming across as something to write sympathetically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T17:25:04-08:00","id":1474146,"title":"","content":"That wasn't &quot;the core&quot; back when I first started playing. The system was much more flexible than that. You could make a game about preserving humanity. You could also make a game about political chess and dominating a city. You could make a game about characters who didn't care about humans at all, not even in the context of wanting to hurt them. Humanity was just one more stat, which the ST could give as much or as little importance as they wanted to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T19:15:42-08:00","id":1474155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474128#post1474128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that that's a bad thing,</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some important caveats tot this, though. Vault products are still &quot;non-canonical&quot;, for what is now a transmedia franchise, and even if the author of a given product wants to cooperate, bringing original Vault creations into the setting is legally tricky. If they like your take on the subject, for example, they can't simply copy it because even if based in their IP, it is <b><u>your</u></b> IP too. Contractual clauses to use this content may work, but they won't be used lightly since this ain't no guarantee of ugly legal battles.<br /> <br /> \u200bI sincerely agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1808\" data-vbnamecard=\"1808\">elmerg</a> here. While they certainly don't want huge doses of bad press theuir focus is on what they can do with the setting as a concise franchise. They're aiming books, movies and video games, so that's about what setting they want to present to media producers, not what setting they want to present to the TTRPG fanbase.<br /> <br /> But I still doubt the question is simply making it easier for transmedia. It isn't. If this is their goal they missed, because a more nuanced Sabbat would be an easier sell in any other media, too. This ain't about making the Sabbat easier to digest, but simply that their core argument, as weird as it sounds, is actually true: they have a vision for the IP and are committed to it.<br /> <br /> Saying that the Sabbat is antithetical to the &quot;core VtM experience&quot; is BS, but actually a BS Paradox fully believe in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T19:23:59-08:00","id":1474157,"title":"","content":"Call me crazy but I think that is putting the cart before the horse. The Sabbat not being part of the &quot;Core VTM experience&quot; may be because, and I go back to the point above, they think it would be far too controversial to sell to the public and new audiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T13:16:26-08:00","id":1474224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474157#post1474157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Call me crazy but I think that is putting the cart before the horse. The Sabbat not being part of the &quot;Core VTM experience&quot; may be because, and I go back to the point above, they think it would be far too controversial to sell to the public and new audiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not an unreasonable theory but I find it personally unlikely. They're almost certainly aware of the massive amounts of Ill will v5s approach to the Sabbat has cultivated so its self defeating in terms of controversy. Furthermore Sabbat his historically been a very popular play choice so the idea new players would be put off doesn't really make sense as we were all new players once.<br /> <br /> Truthfully I don't think their currently is a long term agenda for how to develop the game further considering the original development team for v5 were fired after the incident and the current 'big vision l' for w5 is make it more like forsaken and rid of anything which might be considered problematic. I think they're just stumbling along trying to catch up with initial edition line outline.<br /> <br /> Anybody know why goterix is a woman in that quasi official Sabbat book now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-08-2022, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T15:53:39-08:00","id":1474235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474157#post1474157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Call me crazy but I think that is putting the cart before the horse. The Sabbat not being part of the &quot;Core VTM experience&quot; may be because, and I go back to the point above, they think it would be far too controversial to sell to the public and new audiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will call you crazy, considering that's not at all what Achilli said about the reason and the V5 line direction, but sure, be crazy. It's not because of 'controversy' it's because 'V5 is built around vampires and dealing with Humanity and, by and large, Sabbat throws that away'. Hell, the interview where Achilli said that has been linked multiple times on this board. They have a line vision, where Vampires struggle with Humanity and Sabbat, with their throwing away of Humanity (because let's face it, when people mention Sabbat in the fandom the first thing people think of is Paths of Enlightenment) and everything, doesn't fit that line vision as a playable option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474224#post1474224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anybody know why goterix is a woman in that quasi official Sabbat book now?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not even quasi-official, it's an STV book, and by definition not at all canon or official.<br /> <br /> Anyway, from what the author posted on a Discord and Twitter:<br /> Goratrix (she/they): This was a creative decision that had to do with the ambiguous nature of Goratrix\u2019s gender as presented in the Second Edition of the Sabbat and the First Edition Tremere Clanbook. We took a V5 approach with this book and that meant some lore, especially from Clan Novels and Dark Ages books, were reinterpreted or left in the shadows. In the case of Goratrix, some books presented them as a gay character who was deeply misogynistic and keen on pursuing powerful men or men they had power over. Goratrix is castrated in a ritual, eventually betrays their lovers/friends to the Sabbat, and is ultimately possessed by their old lover/master. This didn\u2019t fit into our vision for the character and we didn\u2019t want to delve into the weeds of those older books. In The Black Hand: Playing the Sabbat their gender is not disclosed, but the name Goratrix does imply a character that prefers feminine presentation and the rest we leave to the Storyteller. Perhaps the old stories are crude propaganda concocted by the conservative and patriarchal Tremere?<br /> In the Antitribu section, the Tremere POV talks about Goratrix as a They. So Goratrix's pronouns in the book are She/They","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 02-08-2022, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T17:23:39-08:00","id":1474241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474235#post1474235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's not even quasi-official, it's an STV book, and by definition not at all canon or official.<br /> <br /> Anyway, from what the author posted on a Discord and Twitter:<br /> Goratrix (she/they): This was a creative decision that had to do with the ambiguous nature of Goratrix\u2019s gender as presented in the Second Edition of the Sabbat and the First Edition Tremere Clanbook. We took a V5 approach with this book and that meant some lore, especially from Clan Novels and Dark Ages books, were reinterpreted or left in the shadows. In the case of Goratrix, some books presented them as a gay character who was deeply misogynistic and keen on pursuing powerful men or men they had power over. Goratrix is castrated in a ritual, eventually betrays their lovers/friends to the Sabbat, and is ultimately possessed by their old lover/master. This didn\u2019t fit into our vision for the character and we didn\u2019t want to delve into the weeds of those older books. In The Black Hand: Playing the Sabbat their gender is not disclosed, but the name Goratrix does imply a character that prefers feminine presentation and the rest we leave to the Storyteller. Perhaps the old stories are crude propaganda concocted by the conservative and patriarchal Tremere?<br /> In the Antitribu section, the Tremere POV talks about Goratrix as a They. So Goratrix's pronouns in the book are She/They</div> </div> </div> </div>Point taken.<br /> <br /> That's certainly an.....interesting interpretation of goratrix and that time he cut off his wily. Is goratrix even a real name?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-08-2022, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T17:56:29-08:00","id":1474242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474241#post1474241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Point taken.<br /> <br /> That's certainly an.....interesting interpretation of goratrix and that time he cut off his wily. Is goratrix even a real name?</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt it. It's a fusion of gore and tricks. It screams made-up-by-a-writer-name.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T18:25:33-08:00","id":1474243,"title":"","content":"If one assumes a Latin origin, the -<i>trix </i>implies a female (though a title?). But it is a made up name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T19:10:00-08:00","id":1474244,"title":"","content":"It's a weird decision to say the least versus making Goratrix a bisexual man who was castrated as part of a ritual and didn't get to regrow anything because Etrius screwed it up.<br /> <br /> Mind you, it's better than Merlinda being 