<div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474235#post1474235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, from what the author posted on a Discord and Twitter:</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you provide a link?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T20:33:56-08:00","id":1474251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474246#post1474246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you provide a link?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I copied what Khaldoun posted on the WoD5 Discord, but here's the twitter thing too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/kkhelil/status/1489041510616207360\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2040737120151625728/WYHy5p-L_400x400.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/kkhelil/status/1489041510616207360\" target=\"_blank\"> Khaldoun Khelil \ud83c\uddf5\ud83c\uddf8\ud83c\udf49\ud83c\udde9\ud83c\uddff (@kkhelil) on X </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/kkhelil/status/1489041510616207360\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/kkhelil/status/1489041510616207360 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> @ethanmcarpenter I addressed your question abt Goratrix's pronouns as I thought its best to be clear about our intentions \ud83e\uddf5 Goratrix (she/they): This was a creative decision that had to do with the ambiguous nature of Goratrix&rsquo;s gender as presented in the Second Edition of 1/5 </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T21:39:59-08:00","id":1474254,"title":"","content":"Here is a quote from House of Tremere, pg. 17: &quot;We knew Goratrix had the magic to eventually grow his P*****s back.&quot;<br /> <br /> He was always depicted as a male. Why now?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T22:20:07-08:00","id":1474256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474241#post1474241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Point taken.<br /> <br /> That's certainly an.....interesting interpretation of goratrix and that time he cut off his wily. Is goratrix even a real name?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Goratrix is supposed to be Gallic/French in terms of background. There are actually a whole host of Gallic names ending in -rix (Vercingetorix, Ambiorix, Dumnorix, and so on). The ending means &quot;king&quot;, and is not too distantly related to the Latin &quot;rex&quot;. I would presume when Goratrix was first created the writers invented a Gallic-sounding name which doesn't actually mean anything, but fits in with the types of names used by powerful Gauls in antiquity. In game terms it's quite easy to justify as a name taken on by Goratrix when he became a mage to emphasise his importance. <br /> <br /> Of course, if your cultural frame of reference extends no further than Harry Potter, you are probably going to assume that a name ending in -rix is female.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T23:07:47-08:00","id":1474258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474254#post1474254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is a quote from House of Tremere, pg. 17: &quot;We knew Goratrix had the magic to eventually grow his P*****s back.&quot;<br /> <br /> He was always depicted as a male. Why now?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect the answer is, &quot;Because it's my book and I have this desire to see it this way.&quot; Perhaps he thought Goratrix was a woman until Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> Sort of like me writing Gary's Kindred, you have a sense of ownership despite it absolutely not being yours.<br /> <br /> Just because you've gamed them for decades at your home table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-09-2022, 02:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T09:29:28-08:00","id":1474289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474235#post1474235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will call you crazy, considering that's not at all what Achilli said about the reason and the V5 line direction, but sure, be crazy. It's not because of 'controversy' it's because 'V5 is built around vampires and dealing with Humanity and, by and large, Sabbat throws that away'. Hell, the interview where Achilli said that has been linked multiple times on this board. They have a line vision, where Vampires struggle with Humanity and Sabbat, with their throwing away of Humanity (because let's face it, when people mention Sabbat in the fandom the first thing people think of is Paths of Enlightenment) and everything, doesn't fit that line vision as a playable option.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, by itself Achili saying isn't the same as it being true. They could very well make decisions based on avoiding backlash and bad press and yet not admit it. The idea that the Sabbat as a playable option harms the theme of struggling with Humanity in the game is also plainly stupid, something already discussed at length around here.<br /> <br /> But that said, their actual decisions and publications do indicate that they believe so and that this belief is indeed the reason behind their decision. They haven't shied of tackling sensible stuff even if to blunder and ask forgiveness later, and that has been working. The game is already about a number of factions with pretty problematic goals and behaviors, the Sabbat simply isn't that big a problem and I don't think they follow the same reasoning that the Sabbat would be more of an issue in a game already about abusive monsters because they're extra violent.<br /> <br /> No. I think they do have a vision for the game that is clear and concise in their minds, and they're just following through. That explains all the decisions perfectly despite anyone's opinion if it is the correct vision or the best strategy to achieve it. Simply put, they don't want the Sabbat in the game, period, not because they fear backlash, but because <u><b>they don't like it</b></u>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474244#post1474244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, it's better than Merlinda being the single female on the council.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Disagree.<br /> <br /> Meerlinda as the only female because they're misogynistic first Millennium Mages makes perfect sense. Tremere's inner circle has always been about his personal preference and playing favorites, it having a biased composition makes perfect sense. It also makes sense with Meerlinda being the most politically savvy of the bunch as she must be to raise there while the men can be talented but to some degree childish. This happens exactly like that in a lot of professional contexts.<br /> <br /> Making Goratrix into a woman is actually a fairly obnoxious decision when not only it contradicts lore, it actually weakens Meerlinda's story and misses several opportunities to work other LGBTQIA+ themes with Goratrix that are more pressing for his themes and more fitting his character. He could even be a trans woman previously in denial, but a woman all along? No, just no. That's just stupid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474256#post1474256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, if your cultural frame of reference extends no further than Harry Potter, you are probably going to assume that a name ending in -rix is female.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I don't know better nowadays, but with my frame of reference at the time being actually a lot of Asterix, the name always sounded masculine to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T09:45:52-08:00","id":1474291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474254#post1474254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was always depicted as a male. Why now?</div> </div> </div> </div>The writer, Khaldoun, seems to believe this makes a statement. But I'm not certain what the statement is or supposed to accomplish.<br /> <br /> That said, I've not read this new material. Does it go into if Tremere is in possession of Goratrix?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T13:20:23-08:00","id":1474321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474254#post1474254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is a quote from House of Tremere, pg. 17: &quot;We knew Goratrix had the magic to eventually grow his P*****s back.&quot;<br /> <br /> He was always depicted as a male. Why now?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Someone more familiar with the word Dominatrix than gaulish &amp; gallo-roman post-celtic naming conventions perhaps?<br /> Seems like a cringy but possible explanation, imho.<br /> <br /> (Ok, i'm joking. Please gods tell that is NOT anywhere near to how that actually happened....)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T14:23:30-08:00","id":1474324,"title":"","content":"&quot;-trix&quot; is a feminine suffix in several Latin derived words. &quot;-rix&quot; is suffix in several Gaulish names. All of the latter that I've seen have a vowel preceding -rix, but I'd guess it was Gaulish if anything, maybe because he was appointed councillor for France and I guessed that he grew up around there. Whatever the etymology, I don't think it makes sense to continue to call out Clan Tremere's patriarchy and change one of its founding mysogynistic patriarchs into a woman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T15:11:56-08:00","id":1474331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474324#post1474324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;-trix&quot; is a feminine suffix in several Latin derived words. &quot;-rix&quot; is suffix in several Gaulish names. All of the latter that I've seen have a vowel preceding -rix, but I'd guess it was Gaulish if anything, maybe because he was appointed councillor for France and I guessed that he grew up around there. Whatever the etymology, I don't think it makes sense to continue to call out Clan Tremere's patriarchy and change one of its founding mysogynistic patriarchs into a woman.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As a random aside, a little bit of homebrew lore i've used a number of time is that, before he was one of Tremere's lieutenants, he was ex-member of House Diedne, origin of his mage name, one of the main factors behind spurring the wizard war against the house and from where came House Tremere's interest in looting their libraries for blood magic secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-09-2022, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T16:59:56-08:00","id":1474336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474289#post1474289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That explains all the decisions perfectly despite anyone's opinion if it is the correct vision or the best strategy to achieve it. Simply put, they don't want the Sabbat in the game, period, not because they fear backlash, but because <u><b>they don't like it</b></u>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think you touch the core issue with a needle, every explanation I've seem from them on the subject has come across as evasive &quot;the plot just led us away.&quot; Or absurd &quot;everyone is Sabbat now because you can play a noddist In the carmarilla.&quot; I think for whatever reason the writters overtly don't want to write Sabbat and the fact they're resisting a certain degree of pressure to do so implies a degree of antithaphy. This is going to be a real problem going forward especially if writters decide they 'don't like' other wod groups.. such as say the technocracy or somesuch. Juvenille approach to a commercial products aside Im forced to wonder how bad this could potentially get before someone gets over themselves and remembers this is a business not your fanon larp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-10-2022, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T19:35:35-08:00","id":1474347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474336#post1474336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you touch the core issue with a needle, every explanation I've seem from them on the subject has come across as evasive &quot;the plot just led us away.&quot; Or absurd &quot;everyone is Sabbat now because you can play a noddist In the carmarilla.&quot; I think for whatever reason the writters overtly don't want to write Sabbat and the fact they're resisting a certain degree of pressure to do so implies a degree of antithaphy. This is going to be a real problem going forward especially if writters decide they 'don't like' other wod groups.. such as say the technocracy or somesuch. Juvenille approach to a commercial aside Im forced to wonder how bad this could potentially get before someone gets over themselves and remembers this is a business not your fanon larp.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually very disappointed with the direction of Mage: The Ascension if the current write-ups are any indication of where they're going. It seems they want to focus on the Nephandi over the Technocracy as antagonists when libel, fascism, and croney capitalism are at their best for being enemies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T20:10:28-08:00","id":1474349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474347#post1474347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm actually very disappointed with the direction of Mage: The Ascension if the current write-ups are any indication of where they're going. It seems they want to focus on the Nephandi over the Technocracy as antagonists when libel, fascism, and croney capitalism are at their best for being enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I can sort of tell in my opinion that's sort of a smart move.<br /> <br /> Judging by how a lot of people spent money on technocracy reloaded as a player's guide for technocracy as well as the fact that no one is complaining about the fact that lore of traditions is dedicating a lot of sections going on about how traditions and technocracy can form alliances I sort of see that as a good mood especially the fact that there isn't the usual fighting about Technocracy vs Traditions that I usually see here and the other places that usually talk about mage during the lore of traditions Kickstarter happening right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T21:13:05-08:00","id":1474352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474349#post1474349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I can sort of tell in my opinion that's sort of a smart move.<br /> <br /> Judging by how a lot of people spent money on technocracy reloaded as a player's guide for technocracy as well as the fact that no one is complaining about the fact that lore of traditions is dedicating a lot of sections going on about how traditions and technocracy can form alliances I sort of see that as a good mood especially the fact that there isn't the usual fighting about Technocracy vs Traditions that I usually see here and the other places that usually talk about mage during the lore of traditions Kickstarter happening right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I get the Good Guy Technocracy has fans but I've always loved them being the bad guys.<br /> <br /> The thing is, I do Technocracy games all the time but I use them to play bad guy games ala Vampire.<br /> <br /> The softening feels like it removed a lot of the Union's edge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T01:28:32-08:00","id":1474356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474124#post1474124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, the controversy will continue in other places with the Hunter: The Reckoning release [no Imbued] and the &quot;Dead Gaia&quot; Werewolf: The Apocalypse. I think they just didn't feel the Sabbat was a fight they could win.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Werewolf game was so bad it ended up in the 10 worst games of the year. <a href=\"https://www.metacritic.com/pictures/worst-video-games-of-2021/8\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.metacritic.com/pictures/...ames-of-2021/8</a><br /> <br /> So Paradox went straight to Hunter. And I guess they will invest on new games instead of books. They just opened up a position for a Licencing Manager, in order to have new videogames. <a href=\"https://twitter.com/worldofdarkness/status/1491414316205379598\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/worldofdarkness/...14316205379598</a><br /> <br /> On a side note, I feel a bit sorry for Onyx. So much hard work in two Kickstarters and now those books are sold by a company more concerned about Power Rangers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T02:34:08-08:00","id":1474357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474336#post1474336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you touch the core issue with a needle, every explanation I've seem from them on the subject has come across as evasive &quot;the plot just led us away.&quot; Or absurd &quot;everyone is Sabbat now because you can play a noddist In the carmarilla.&quot; I think for whatever reason the writters overtly don't want to write Sabbat and the fact they're resisting a certain degree of pressure to do so implies a degree of antithaphy. This is going to be a real problem going forward especially if writters decide they 'don't like' other wod groups.. such as say the technocracy or somesuch. Juvenille approach to a commercial products aside Im forced to wonder how bad this could potentially get before someone gets over themselves and remembers this is a business not your fanon larp.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The WOD leader is Justin Achilli, who is far from being a &quot;juvenile&quot; author or someone concerned with his own &quot;fanon LARP&quot;. Along with our favourite uberWOD Nerd Matthew Dawkins, he is probably the most knowledgeable WOD loremaster out there.<br /> <br /> Mind you, Martin Ericsson and his team, who were accused of being juvenile fanon LARPers, were very keen on using A LOT of references to earlier canon in the first V5 products, which are much more nuanced in latest OPP and ParaWolf products.<br /> <br /> As much as one cannot agree with their artistic vision, I wouldn't say that the IP is managed by people who don't know business (especially now, that is directly in the hands of the former WW Vampire-in-Chief under scrutiny from a world-class videogame producer) or who treat the franchise as a pet fan project.<br /> <br /> Something has probably happened between the Chechenya backlash and now: I'd say that V5 was meant to &quot;bring all the WOD together&quot;, from old Vampire to Requiem fans, like D&amp;D 5th did. However, V20 unexpectedly became their Pathfinder, and they re-focused on making V5 more &quot;a clean slate&quot; to bring new gamers in. In doing so, they are making choices, even drastic ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 02-10-2022, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T04:55:33-08:00","id":1474364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474347#post1474347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm actually very disappointed with the direction of Mage: The Ascension if the current write-ups are any indication of where they're going. It seems they want to focus on the Nephandi over the Technocracy as antagonists when libel, fascism, and croney capitalism are at their best for being enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that's a bad thing, if anything the union is probably more topical than ever. Although personally I percieve the union as more a morally ambigiois technocratic neo Liberal obligarch than fascist the union seems to frown on modern right wing developments as divisive and disruptive to scheduling &quot;All races, creeds and peoples have value and a place in out world....and we will ensure you are aware of both.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T05:01:50-08:00","id":1474365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bb