y from them being a mystical cult-like boogeyman you know little about and. Not that anything is stopping you from homebrewing the few needed alterations for Paths.<br /> <br /> They still have officially promoted Sabbat STV materials, and as you know, one of their writers even published their own guide on the STV. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T09:20:05-08:00","id":1474377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474376#post1474376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can disagree with him all you want, it is still non-sensical to dismiss him as childish or as if it was some sort of personal vendetta against the Sabbat. And it's likewise ridiculous to assume that a company doesn't want to make money.<br /> <br /> They just thought <i>non-officially</i> playable Sabbat was a better choice for their vision of 5th Edition, that view being that having them be playable would take away from them being a mystical cult-like boogeyman you know little about and. Not that anything is stopping you from homebrewing the few needed alterations for Paths.<br /> <br /> They still have officially promoted Sabbat STV materials, and as you know, one of their writers even published their own guide on the STV.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have seen at least a couple of people be fine with the whole Sabbat being nonplayable though that doesn't mean that the people that wanna play Sabbat are wrong, the fact that they allowed the release of STV material to play Sabbat means they are completely fine with it especially seeing as its got more positive reviews and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T11:36:20-08:00","id":1474382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474377#post1474377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have seen at least a couple of people be fine with the whole Sabbat being nonplayable though that doesn't mean that the people that wanna play Sabbat are wrong, the fact that they allowed the release of STV material to play Sabbat means they are completely fine with it especially seeing as its got more positive reviews and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly that's because STV content isn't policed for content, except for whether or not it fits the STV rules like allowed logos or replacing the need for a core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T11:47:51-08:00","id":1474383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474376#post1474376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can disagree with him all you want, it is still non-sensical to dismiss him as childish or as if it was some sort of personal vendetta against the Sabbat. And it's likewise ridiculous to assume that a company doesn't want to make money.<br /> <br /> They just thought <i>non-officially</i> playable Sabbat was a better choice for their vision of 5th Edition, that view being that having them be playable would take away from them being a mystical cult-like boogeyman you know little about and. Not that anything is stopping you from homebrewing the few needed alterations for Paths.<br /> <br /> They still have officially promoted Sabbat STV materials, and as you know, one of their writers even published their own guide on the STV. </div> </div> </div> </div>I'm unconvinced of your argument as it relies on the assumption that companies and their employees are guaranteed to make logical benificial decisions, historically white wolf has a tendancy towards eccentric behaviour with odd motivations and in a world were the tv franchise of the decade imploded at the finish line because the showrunners got restless it's hardly a stretch . Vendetta is a strong word I'd use antipathy which is still frankly a very silly approach to your bread and butter. Theirs literally no indication that making them non playable was a good move. <br /> <br /> The ongoing presence of disgruntled Sabbat players indicates otherwise. Yes but they completely failed at that and it's probably impossible to do. The only really 'mysterious' aspect of the Sabbat is they usually engage on asymmetrical tactics now and the plot holes <br /> <br /> Homebrewing is damning with faint praise","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-10-2022, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T12:26:23-08:00","id":1474385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474383#post1474383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm unconvinced of your argument as it relies on the assumption that companies and their employees are guaranteed to make logical rational decisions, historically white wolf has a tendancy towards eccentric behaviour with odd motivations and in a world were the tv franchise of the decade imploded at the finish line because the showrunners got restless it's hardly a stretch . Vendetta is a strong word I'd use antipathy which is still frankly a very silly approach to your bread and butter. Theirs literally no indication that making them non playable was a good move.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why, <i>historically</i>, White Wolf hasn't existed for the past 3 years, after that whole controversy, and the WoD IP is run by Paradox, with far more oversight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474383#post1474383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ongoing presence of disgruntled Sabbat players indicates otherwise. Yes but they completely failed at that and it's probably impossible to do. The only really 'mysterious' aspect of the Sabbat is they usually engage on asymmetrical tactics now and the plot holes<br /> <br /> Homebrewing is damning with faint praise</div> </div> </div> </div>Indicates what? That the book not made for &quot;Sabbat players&quot; didn't satisfy &quot;Sabbat players&quot;? You can't really fault them for something that wasn't their goal at all. You can disagree with the decision, but not criticize them for not failing at something that wasn't their goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T13:13:58-08:00","id":1474388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474352#post1474352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I get the Good Guy Technocracy has fans but I've always loved them being the bad guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that this is a change in how most fans want the Technocracy to be.<br /> <br /> Original Techy works on the assumption that Fascism = Modernity, and is a symbol of Luddite ideals the fandom never bought as much as the authors and shied from it even more with time. So much so that this movement started already in 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> Like it or not, most people don't see very well the idea of the Technocracy as representing such things all the while it defends proper and safe science and collective development (because they do, while the Traditions focus on individual development), so changing focus to the Nefandi in this regard is also an old strategy already (implied, for example, in the Syndicate R&amp;D shenanigans).<br /> <br /> Personally I think they should develop more the role of Threat Null, that is already a mix of parody and reference to Old Techy, but in a way that makes more sense than just proper academy and formal institutions being universally tools of evil and our future depending on our timely salvation by mediums and deluded charlatans.<br /> <br /> I think we could even have a very interesting game if the focus changed to both Trads and Techy fending off a renewed War between Threat Null and a similar Ultra-Luddite Traditions-equivalent. In this sense I do agree that focusing on the Nefandi is kind of dull and too much on the steps of Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474357#post1474357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as one cannot agree with their artistic vision, I wouldn't say that the IP is managed by people who don't know business (especially now, that is directly in the hands of the former WW Vampire-in-Chief under scrutiny from a world-class videogame producer) or who treat the franchise as a pet fan project.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I do agree that just slandering their preparedness isn't a good or accurate take on the matter, praising them as if it meant they're not making mistakes isn't either.<br /> <br /> AFAIK Achilli is very knowledgeable about Vampire, but also very biased towards personal preferences. Less now than in the past, and in no extreme terms, but still. The upper management of Paradox demonstrated a very defined vision about the game at least since the actual core publication, which is both good and bad.<br /> <br /> It certainly isn't managed as just a pet project. Quite the contrary, it is the most ambitious and business-oriented management team WoD ever had, and this isn't bad <i>per se</i>. But it doesn't mean they won't commit mistakes or that their vision don't have problems, not just their artistic vision, but their business strategy.<br /> <br /> The whole Sabbat thing in the end boils down to it. They don't like the Sabbat, they don't want it in their vision of the setting as anything remotely playable. Why it is so is irrelevant, either personal preference or business strategy boil down to the same. I fully disagree that it has anything to do with Chechnya, because this stance was actually very clear since the core. The only change was they even deciding to make a Sabbat book in the first place, and even this I think had more to do with distancing the Gehenna War from their initial lore that it happened in an undefined Middle East where, surprise, there are also WoD players.<br /> <br /> Now, from what I get from their vision and stance on the matter and how they conduct their business, I <b><u>do</u></b> think they're making a series of mistakes, not because I think fans should have everything they want, but because from a franchise perspective I think they're cutting off avenues for exploration without really obtaining the benefits they seek with a better defined and coherent setting. And sometimes they're putting aside complexities that are responsible for giving the setting its coherence in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474385#post1474385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indicates what? That the book not made for &quot;Sabbat players&quot; didn't satisfy &quot;Sabbat players&quot;? You can't really fault them for something that wasn't their goal at all. You can disagree with the decision, but not criticize them for not failing at something that wasn't their goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't defend their decision to not make a product because fans making it is somehow a better move like you said earlier.<br /> <br /> The Vault isn't official, canonical lore. Despite they getting a cut, licensed product with little oversight is not the same as corporate product. It isn't a good decision, it is a non decision. They didn't promoted the community work to bring the Sabbat to the game, they decided that the game has no playable Sabbat, period. And they believing this is a smart decision does not mean it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T13:22:53-08:00","id":1474389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm unconvinced of your argument as it relies on the assumption that companies and their employees are guaranteed to make logical benificial decisions, historically white wolf has a tendancy towards eccentric behaviour with odd motivations and in a world were the tv franchise of the decade imploded at the finish line because the showrunners got restless it's hardly a stretch . Vendetta is a strong word I'd use antipathy which is still frankly a very silly approach to your bread and butter. Theirs literally no indication that making them non playable was a good move. </div> </div> </div>You believed D&amp;D when they said that the final stretch of Game of Thrones was bad 'because we rushed it'? They pretty clearly just had no clue on how to do anything if they didn't have to books to work from. As evidence, look at things from earlier seasons like what they did to the Dorne storyline. Like when the sand snakes were actually vying to be the ones to commit a serious taboo and be a kin slayer who killed their cousin as their dad was spinning in his grave over them killing family. That was just an excuse the two of them made up because its less damaging then admitting 'we are nothing without George R.R. Martin doing most of the work for us'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T13:39:45-08:00","id":1474392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474385#post1474385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is why, <i>historically</i>, White Wolf hasn't existed for the past 3 years, after that whole controversy, and the WoD IP is run by Paradox, with far more oversight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Indicates what? That the book not made for &quot;Sabbat players&quot; didn't satisfy &quot;Sabbat players&quot;? You can't really fault them for something that wasn't their goal at all. You can disagree with the decision, but not criticize them for not failing at something that wasn't their goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you wish, wod products as a historical product and I don't think Paradox put a nix on the Sabbat as theirs literally no evidence for it.<br /> <br /> That not creating Sabbat playable material is an error. I can certainly fault them for bad ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-10-2022, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T13:59:56-08:00","id":1474394,"title":"","content":"So, correct me if I am wrong, but didn't they sack the whole team recently and make a brand new one over some outrage involving Chechnya related content in a book? Seems like the kind of thing that could really change up the game line vision when it comes to things like 'the Sabbat are not going to be playable'. Or was this a statement from the current team?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T14:19:15-08:00","id":1474395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474394#post1474394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, correct me if I am wrong, but didn't they sack the whole team recently and make a brand new one over some outrage involving Chechnya related content in a book? Seems like the kind of thing that could really change up the game line vision when it comes to things like 'the Sabbat are not going to be playable'. Or was this a statement from the current team?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They didn't sack the whole team, Martin Erricson left and the whole white wolf got restructured and integrated into paradox interactive and had a paradox vice president manage them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T15:25:09-08:00","id":1474397,"title":"","content":"Ah, my bad, the article I had read just said WW had been disbanded so I didn't realize Paradox had kept them for development assets for the in house team.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T15:43:20-08:00","id":1474398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474388#post1474388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is that this is a change in how most fans want the Technocracy to be.<br /> <br /> Original Techy works on the assumption that Fascism = Modernity, and is a symbol of Luddite ideals the fandom never bought as much as the authors and shied from it even more with time. So much so that this movement started already in 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> Like it or not, most people don't see very well the idea of the Technocracy as representing such things all the while it defends proper and safe science and collective development (because they do, while the Traditions focus on individual development), so changing focus to the Nefandi in this regard is also an old strategy already (implied, for example, in the Syndicate R&amp;D shenanigans).<br /> <br /> Personally I think they should develop more the role of Threat Null, that is already a mix of parody and reference to Old Techy, but in a way that makes more sense than just proper academy and formal institutions being universally tools of evil and our future depending on our timely salvation by mediums and deluded charlatans.<br /> <br /> I think we could even have a very interesting game if the focus changed to both Trads and Techy fending off a renewed War between Threat Null and a similar Ultra-Luddite Traditions-equivalent. In this sense I do agree that focusing on the Nefandi is kind of dull and too much on the steps of Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always felt this was an issue with the fundamental conception of the Technocracy and I feel like there were two ways of resolving it. The problem with the Technocracy is it is a World of Darkness and if you had people who believed in racial equality, science, and the promotion of social justice among the poor...THE WORLD WOULD NOT LOOK LIKE IT DOES NOW. The Technocracy can either rule the world behind the scenes, be effective, or be progressive but it certainly cannot be all three.<br /> <br /> The solution is one of two things:<br /> <br /> 1. The Technocracy is supportive of racial heirarchies, looter capitalism, disinformation, and a boot on the face of humanity forever.<br /> <br /> 2. The Technocracy is actually a bunch of progressives with guns but not nearly as powerful.<br /> <br /> 2# is fine...if they're the protagonists.<br /> <br /> But we I supported 1# because I believe the Technocracy would always side with big oil over clean energy because I'm the anarchist Goth market for the classic WOD.<br /> <br /> It's weirdly a lot less of a disconnect in V:TM and Werewolf because &quot;The Man&quot; is objectively evil there.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm not going to whine about it. They made their choice and you just go with the flow. Sometimes you like changes to a setting, sometimes you don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-10-2022, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T17:35:19-08:00","id":1474403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474397#post1474397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, my bad, the article I had read just said WW had been disbanded so I didn't realize Paradox had kept them for development assets for the in house team.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also this has some time already, the Sabbat book and the statements in discussion are already by the current team.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474398#post1474398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always felt this was an issue with the fundamental conception of the Technocracy and I feel like there were two ways of resolving it. The problem with the Technocracy is it is a World of Darkness and if you had people who believed in racial equality, science, and the promotion of social justice among the poor...THE WORLD WOULD NOT LOOK LIKE IT DOES NOW. The Technocracy can either rule the world behind the scenes, be effective, or be progressive but it certainly cannot be all three.<br /> <br /> The solution is one of two things:<br /> <br /> 1. The Technocracy is supportive of racial heirarchies, looter capitalism, disinformation, and a boot on the face of humanity forever.<br /> <br /> 2. The Technocracy is actually a bunch of progressives with guns but not nearly as powerful.<br /> <br /> 2# is fine...if they're the protagonists.<br /> <br /> But we I supported 1# because I believe the Technocracy would always side with big oil over clean energy because I'm the anarchist Goth market for the classic WOD.<br /> <br /> It's weirdly a lot less of a disconnect in V:TM and Werewolf because &quot;The Man&quot; is objectively evil there.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm not going to whine about it. They made their choice and you just go with the flow. Sometimes you like changes to a setting, sometimes you don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right here, the point is just that #2 got a lot more traction very early in the game's life. That's just to say that in this particular case they're following through an older and more popular decision, and one that gels with most players that like the faction, in opposition to what they did to the Sabbat that wasn't at all well received by Sabbat players.<br /> <br /> Threat Null could easily be applied to solve this issue. With access to Control's resources and conditioning they could wrestle the power from post-Guide Technocracy and remake pre-Guide Technocracy under less Luddite assumptions, post-Guide weakened but available as PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T19:01:01-08:00","id":1474408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474388#post1474388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Original Techy works on the assumption that Fascism = Modernity, and is a symbol of Luddite ideals the fandom never bought as much as the authors and shied from it even more with time. So much so that this movement started already in 2nd ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to chase rabbits too much, but of the five original lines, four were about fighting the system and raging against the machine; <i>Werewolf, Mage, Wraith </i>and <i>Changeling</i>. The system was out to get you, one way or another, in each game line. Naturally this gave the bad guys a fascist tone. Only in <i>VtM </i>wasn't about fighting the system or raging against the machine not really, because vampires - Camarilla, Anarch, Inconnu, Sabbat - are the system at its most heartless, callow and predatory.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T20:47:04-08:00","id":1474413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474408#post1474408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't want to chase rabbits too much, but of the five original lines, four were about fighting the system and raging against the machine; <i>Werewolf, Mage, Wraith </i>and <i>Changeling</i>. The system was out to get you, one way or another, in each game line. Naturally this gave the bad guys a fascist tone. Only in <i>VtM </i>wasn't about fighting the system or raging against the machine not really, because vampires - Camarilla, Anarch, Inconnu, Sabbat - are the system at its most heartless, callow and predatory.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a pretty easy and surprisingly effective way of doing it. You take cyberpunk and replace the tech with magic.<br /> <br /> You replace the corpos with soulless pale bloodrinking monsters.<br /> <br /> The Elders are the Corpos.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T20:50:30-08:00","id":1474414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474403#post1474403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Threat Null could easily be applied to solve this issue. With access to Control's resources and conditioning they could wrestle the power from post-Guide Technocracy and remake pre-Guide Technocracy under less Luddite assumptions, post-Guide weakened but available as PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, you could probably just get away with using Threat Null and Nephandi as antagonists, if you wanted a third set of antagonists maybe add in staunch hardliners from both sides, basically Technocratic people that are firm believers of the pogrom and believed and benefited from being enemies with the Traditions as well as Tradition groups that splintered hard from the mainline who are firm believers of fighting the technocrats and have the mind set of &quot;If you're with them then you count as the enemy.&quot; Peppered about.<br /> <br /> As for the whole enemy of the system thing what would demon, Kuejin. mummy and Hunter be considered as?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 02-10-2022, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T14:15:50-08:00","id":1474438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474408#post1474408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to chase rabbits too much, but of the five original lines, four were about fighting the system and raging against the machine; <i>Werewolf, Mage, Wraith </i>and <i>Changeling</i>. The system was out to get you, one way or another, in each game line. Naturally this gave the bad guys a fascist tone. Only in <i>VtM </i>wasn't about fighting the system or raging against the machine not really, because vampires - Camarilla, Anarch, Inconnu, Sabbat - are the system at its most heartless, callow and predatory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire isn't an exception. Both 1st and 2nd ed <b><u>cores</u></b> have a strong subtext that the PCs can chose to fight the system and that this is actually the &quot;good&quot; path. You're not required to do it, but the personal horror elements do have a solution where you improve your actual existence and gain mechanical benefits if you refuse to play the rigged game of Jyhad, and you can improve the world by fighting the system.<br /> <br /> For several reasons this subtext becomes ever more subtle as the game grows with supplements and becomes more complex, which isn't a bad thing, but the subtext is always there. Only 5th ed has a heavier hand on stating vampires as almost irredeemable, but even there it is just <i>almost</i>.<br /> <br /> The specific problem with Mage is how much the Luddite undertone of the game got increased and merged with this notion of <i>the system</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474414#post1474414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, you could probably just get away with using Threat Null and Nephandi as antagonists, if you wanted a third set of antagonists maybe add in staunch hardliners from both sides, basically Technocratic people that are firm believers of the pogrom and believed and benefited from being enemies with the Traditions as well as Tradition groups that splintered hard from the mainline who are firm believers of fighting the technocrats and have the mind set of &quot;If you're with them then you count as the enemy.&quot; Peppered about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Threat Null could be merged easily with Techy hardliners and keep most main Technocratic assets, in fact assume control of many of them completely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T15:09:59-08:00","id":1474444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474438#post1474438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The specific problem with Mage is how much the Luddite undertone of the game got increased and merged with this notion of <i>the system</i></div> </div> </div> </div>A friend of mine had the view that Mage: The Ascension's critics and supporters on the issue were also talking past one another as the two people weren't hearing the other's arguments. It was possibly a very good example of the game's themes that they could see the exact same material and come to completely different conclusions about what each side represented. By contrast, V:TM and W:TA had far less issues about what both sides were about.<br /> <br /> The critics of the Traditions vs. Technocracy conflict tend to see the matter as having a strong Luddite bias with conspiratorial overtones. I've once seen the Traditions described as the &quot;lunatic religious fringe, anti-vaxxers, and alternative medicine nuts worried about the Democrats.&quot; They think the work takes a strong anti-Modernist tone to it.<br /> <br /> The proponents of the Traditions vs. Technocracy conflict see it as indigineous people as well as underground persecuted peoples versus fascist corporate Far Right authoritarianism. The Traditions aren't anti-science to them because the &quot;true scientists&quot; are the Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts representing open source free research versus Big Pharma/Big Tech.<br /> <br /> It's not that the two sides disagree, it's that the two sides are not even having the same argument. In W:TA the werewolves ARE aggressively Luddite ecoterrorists but Pentex is an embodiment of corporate fascism and arguably religious environmental disdain (&quot;we're the chosen so we don't care what happens to the planet and we'll usher it to its doom&quot;--which is a stretch but not an utter one). So you know that the werewolves are incredibly flawed but still on the right side of things. No one is arguing Pentex isn't the bad guys after all.<br /> <br /> Both sides above are angry and full of venom at the Far Right and their effect on the world but they each think the OTHER side of the Technocracy vs. Traditions vibe is the Far Right.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I overthink this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T17:32:39-08:00","id":1474458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474444#post1474444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe I overthink this.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's exactly what it is, and that's the problem.<br /> <br /> Punk literature isn't Luddite <i>per se</i>, but it does have some light Luddite overtones not because of discredit for science, but discredit for the institutions that create it. So it is only natural that the games also have such overtones. It isn't applied equally everywhere, though, because context matters. Partially the very point is that <i><u>classic</u></i> Punk didn't aged well through the 90's.<br /> <br /> I think a big part off the problem is the distinction between collectivist perceptions and individualist perceptions. Punk has a strong emphasis on individualism, not in a sense of greed but personal freedom and expression, and Mage touches particularly this subject with the Technocracy representing mass indoctrination.<br /> <br /> The problem being that proper science is far more a collective process and industrialization having some collective benefits (like cheap products far more affordable) that don't follow well on the trope and end up in the Technocratic side of things squarely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T18:02:12-08:00","id":1474462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474458#post1474458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">No, that's exactly what it is, and that's the problem.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Punk literature isn't Luddite <i>per se</i>, but it does have some light Luddite overtones not because of discredit for science, but discredit for the institutions that create it. So it is only natural that the games also have such overtones. It isn't applied equally everywhere, though, because context matters. Partially the very point is that <i><u>classic</u></i> Punk didn't aged well through the 90's.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think a big part off the problem is the distinction between collectivist perceptions and individualist perceptions. Punk has a strong emphasis on individualism, not in a sense of greed but personal freedom and expression, and Mage touches particularly this subject with the Technocracy representing mass indoctrination.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The problem being that proper science is far more a collective process and industrialization having some collective benefits (like cheap products far more affordable) that don't follow well on the trope and end up in the Technocratic side of things squarely.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Someone on another rpg site did a talk about original Luddites were complaining about</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sci-fi writer Cory Doctorow in which he argues that the perception of them as technophobic is libelous and that their actions were actually driven by outrage concerning the manner in which not only were profits derived from their labour reinvested in technology that destroyed their traditional livelihood, but that they had to continue in that labour under conditions that now included lower pay, longer hours, and a very high chance of being maimed or killed. He also draws attention to deeper implications of the advent of textile technology; of how land enclosure to produce sheep herds for wool destroyed many communities, and the demand for cotton facilitated the slave trade. The central thesis of the argument is that the actual Luddites should be looked at to inspire the question of not merely what machines do, but who they do it for and to.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Though the modern and usage term is way different from this now but this would be sort of relevant.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474444#post1474444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not that the two sides disagree, it's that the two sides are not even having the same argument. In W:TA the werewolves ARE aggressively Luddite ecoterrorists but Pentex is an embodiment of corporate fascism and arguably religious environmental disdain (&quot;we're the chosen so we don't care what happens to the planet and we'll usher it to its doom&quot;--which is a stretch but not an utter one). So you know that the werewolves are incredibly flawed but still on the right side of things. No one is arguing Pentex isn't the bad guys after all.<br /> <br /> Both sides above are angry and full of venom at the Far Right and their effect on the world but they each think the OTHER side of the Technocracy vs. Traditions vibe is the Far Right.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I overthink this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny enough in the same thread Matthew Dawkins had this to say about the whole deal<br /> <br /> Matthew Dawkins<br /> The old Traditions as luddites vs Technocracy as progressives argument of prior editions is something that always captivated me when I first got into WoD, but I'm glad it's moved beyond that in M20, honestly.<br /> <br /> I am unsure what M5 is going to do about Technocracy and Traditions in terms of these things but the people working on M20 aren't really planning on doing what was said above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T18:03:42-08:00","id":1474463,"title":"","content":"The people who most talk about respecting tradition, and who have the most contempt for science, are rightwingers. So it's always been a stretch to call the Traditions leftwing. However, the Technocrats contain groups that are thinly veiled metaphors for spy networks and big business, so it's a stretch to call them leftwing either. <br /> <br /> This results in what really amounts to a battle between populist-right and establishment-right, with the left nowhere to be found.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T18:50:26-08:00","id":1474465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474463#post1474463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The people who most talk about respecting tradition, and who have the most contempt for science, are rightwingers. So it's always been a stretch to call the Traditions leftwing. However, the Technocrats contain groups that are thinly veiled metaphors for spy networks and big business, so it's a stretch to call them leftwing either.<br /> <br /> This results in what really amounts to a battle between populist-right and establishment-right, with the left nowhere to be found.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that the Traditions are made of oppressed minorities and victims of colonialism as well as are primarily NOT American in origin also kind of skews people who want to view it exclusively through the lens of American or even Latin American politics.<br /> <br /> I mean, a traditionalist Maori activist like Temurera Morrison is going to see something very different about the game than someone who thinks the Traditionalists are anti-vaxxers.<br /> <br /> For example: The Technocracy vs. the Traditions in, say, China right now would probably look very different when talking about the crushing of religious minorities.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> But yes, I think the major thing is WHAT The Union and Traditions are depends greatly on the ST and there's ample justification for both sides of the argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-11-2022, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T19:57:06-08:00","id":1474472,"title":"","content":"Part of the confusion is also the way the groups were constructed in a way that is at odds with their real-life counterparts.<br /> <br /> In fact, the historical way the groups were set up in the Victorian era fits better than the Traditions vs the Technocrats.<br /> <br /> The establishment is an alliance of corporations, religious zealots, the spy apparatus and has never stopped being allies in the real world. Science never conquered anything and remains mostly begging for crumbs from the establishment. The Victorian arrangement of allies never really changed, but the game pretends that there was a massive realignment that never happened.<br /> <br /> A realistic arrangement of alliances would be the Syndicate, the Celestial Chorus, and the NWO as the establishment, and everyone else as a disorganized mess, sometimes rebelling, something begging the Establishment for crumbs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 02-11-2022, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T20:31:57-08:00","id":1474474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474472#post1474472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A realistic arrangement of alliances would be the Syndicate, the Celestial Chorus, and the NWO as the establishment, and everyone else as a disorganized mess, sometimes rebelling, something begging the Establishment for crumbs.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Celestial Choir also suffers from the fact that it bears no resemblance to fanon's conception of them. Fanon's take being they're dangerous fanatics and fundamentalists due to many gamers being hostile to organized religion. It's actually an ecumanist liberal Unitarian philosophy. Something no one in the Right would ever approve of and have frequently burned or killed the equivalent of historically. The Technocracy really needs the Knights Templar to still be a member. Which is why the Seers of the Throne still have their equivalent.<br /> <br /> Also, Iteration X isn't just &quot;science&quot; as I always thought it represented the Miltary Industrial Complex and war machinery as their sole product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-12-2022, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T01:50:53-08:00","id":1474486,"title":"","content":"The <b>Technocracy vs Traditions</b> divide is a<b> Mainstream vs Counterculture</b> conflict: it's in clear debt to the great cultural and political trends of the 70s and 80s: it remained long relevant, as anti-globalization movements were an important source of politicization until the recent crisis.<br /> <br /> Now that anti-vaxxers, racists and fundamentalists are joined in a new political bloc fighting against both left-wing countercultures and the mainstream neoliberal order, it seems of course outdated.<br /> <br /> I think both Traditions and Technocracy would be less interesting if their respective bad and good angles were erased, but some sort of shake up could be imagined.<br /> <br /> If the 90s and 2000s had people fighting against &quot;<i>the End of History</i>&quot; and the one-and-only Truth, now we have the problem that there's no coherent and accepted Truth, and the world is seemingly going to hell because no one can really agree on how to act.<br /> <br /> I could imagine a setting shake up where Consensus is falling apart, with a growing number of spontaneous Awakenings that lead unprepared people to Quiet.<br /> <br /> Traditions and Conventions could split up between:<br /> <br /> <i>-Those who think the Earth is ultimately doomed, and try to save what is worth, by facing the Umbra (a libertarian &quot;right&quot;), ranging from Syndicate and Void Engineers to Virtual Adepts<br /> -Those who wish to retake control by forcefully creating a new Consensus (an authoritarian &quot;centre&quot;), with Hermetics, Euthanatos, NWO and Batini, perhaps the Templars<br /> -Those who wish to protect their communities and personal identities (a libertarian &quot;left&quot;), from Dreamspeakers to Disparates<br /> -You could also have a neutral faction that tries to heal the rifts of reality, led by Unitarian Choristers and benign Progenitors.</i><br /> <br /> With the Nephandi as the common threat, and the game emphasizing the agency of Orphans.<br /> <br /> It's a very rough draft, but you could play up on the growing tensions between Traditions and the Rogue Council, or the looming Techcnoratic Civil War.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T02:00:09-08:00","id":1474488,"title":"","content":"Personally I've never really had with the union as leftish wing with some altruistic traits. I actually think this is quite topical with the emergence of modern silicon vally business' were they show some interest in environmentalism and 'support' blm but God help you if you want to form a union.<br /> <br /> Guys like Jeff bezos and Disneys sudden enthusiasm for pride spring to mind.<br /> <br /> It also allows for some moral ambiguities which I always enjoy, it becomes quite awkward if the local syndicate member is a first nations captain of industry and your white hermetic ass has never had a real job because you're a magic republican.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T02:14:42-08:00","id":1474489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474488#post1474488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I've never really had with the union as leftish wing with some altruistic traits. I actually think this is quite topical with the emergence of modern silicon vally business' were they show some interest in environmentalism and 'support' blm but God help you if you want to form a union.<br /> <br /> Guys like Jeff bezos and Disneys sudden enthusiasm for pride spring to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the biggest issue is there's a big honking gap in the Technocracy and Traditions conflict is the Technocracy is progressives and the Traditions are rebels out to free themselves from being, well genocided by ideological fanatics. There should be a third faction that benefits from the oppression of the masses and their ignorance. Not quite the Nephandi who are DESTROY EVERYTHING but something like the Seers.<br /> <br /> The people who are like, &quot;Racism is great because it continues distracting the public while I manipulate from behind the scenes.&quot;<br /> <br /> The 1st Edition Union was like that and people called it unrealistic and stupid. However, we now know that there's plenty of capitalist groups trhat donate vast amounts of money to Far Right causes because they do actually use it as a bait and switch.<br /> <br /> I feel weirdly that Pentex should also be a Mage villain as they fill a lot of the void that Mage has and would be a perfect foe for the Union AND traditions. It would actually give the Union an opponent they can fight on their level. Threat Null is interesting but you'd need to fully embrace it as a setting pillar/antagonist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also allows for some moral ambiguities which I always enjoy, it becomes quite awkward if the local syndicate member is a first nations captain of industry and your white hermetic ass has never had a real job because you're a magic republican. </div> </div> </div>Which gets into the whole Edition Wars. Because if you're a 2nd Edition Technocrat even up to the GUIDE TO THE TECHNOCRACY, the First Nations Syndicate member wants to murder you and your lily white ass for the fact you believe in your religion and want to prove its existence to the public by making potions that cure AIDs.<br /> <br /> The post-racial Technocracy just becomes WEIRD.<br /> <br /> Which is perhaps why the Ascension War was cancelled.<br /> <br /> *cue Idris Elba gif*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-12-2022, 05:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T07:16:30-08:00","id":1474495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474489#post1474489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like the biggest issue is there's a big honking gap in the Technocracy and Traditions conflict is the Technocracy is progressives and the Traditions are rebels out to free themselves from being, well genocided by ideological fanatics. There should be a third faction that benefits from the oppression of the masses and their ignorance. Not quite the Nephandi who are DESTROY EVERYTHING but something like the Seers.<br /> <br /> The people who are like, &quot;Racism is great because it continues distracting the public while I manipulate from behind the scenes.&quot;<br /> <br /> The 1st Edition Union was like that and people called it unrealistic and stupid. However, we now know that there's plenty of capitalist groups trhat donate vast amounts of money to Far Right causes because they do actually use it as a bait and switch.<br /> <br /> I feel weirdly that Pentex should also be a Mage villain as they fill a lot of the void that Mage has and would be a perfect foe for the Union AND traditions. It would actually give the Union an opponent they can fight on their level. Threat Null is interesting but you'd need to fully embrace it as a setting pillar/antagonist.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which gets into the whole Edition Wars. Because if you're a 2nd Edition Technocrat even up to the GUIDE TO THE TECHNOCRACY, the First Nations Syndicate member wants to murder you and your lily white ass for the fact you believe in your religion and want to prove its existence to the public by making potions that cure AIDs.<br /> <br /> The post-racial Technocracy just becomes WEIRD.<br /> <br /> Which is perhaps why the Ascension War was cancelled.<br /> <br /> *cue Idris Elba gif*</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally I've never been particulary keen on that angle or mages, I always preffered the idea that racism is an etension of mankinds intrisicaly tribalistic tendancies fused with anachronisms of early modern imperialism (or technocratic imperialism if you like) which the powers of wod react to rather than instigate more an angle of exploitation than deliberate campaign. worryingly the disparate alliance seems to be a more obvious candidate with it's multiple ethno centric traditions and extreme territorialism. This is quite the can of worms on reflection.<br /> <br /> Or maybe that first nation syndicate member is a corrupt piece of shit who does actually benifit his local community<br /> <br /> It's funny you mention pentex I was talking with a mate of mine and speculating that modern pentex companies might have rainbow logos during pride month and a likable twitter with snarky wendy style quips while still perpetrating homophobia, racism and sexism at an institutional level in old boy mindset. When I think on it W20's desire for change in setting is particularly perplexing as if anything it's more topical than ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-17-2022, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T08:58:41-08:00","id":1474503,"title":"","content":"I admit I'm not a fan of the Disparate Alliance. It feels like someone thought the Traditions were something else and then made the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Because, &quot;group of people with nothing in common who want to be left alone to do their magic in peace banded together for mutual survival&quot; is pretty much how I always ran the Nine.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T09:15:52-08:00","id":1474504,"title":"","content":"I think the Disparates are rooted in the idea that the Hermetics are techocrat types who only became rebels because they lost. And that, further, the Hermetics dominate the Traditions. Whether that's true or not is open to debate, but that seems to be the core idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T12:59:51-08:00","id":1474510,"title":"","content":"With respect, should this conversation be in another forum?<br /> <br /> More on topic for this thread, what do you think of the V5 titles on the Vault/ What kind of VtM material do you want to see on the Vault?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T15:22:30-08:00","id":1474524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474510#post1474510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With respect, should this conversation be in another forum?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was tempted to move the posts to, &quot;handling other factions in Vampire&quot; or just move it to the Mage forum as its own thread but I think the conversation has wound down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More on topic for this thread, what do you think of the V5 titles on the Vault/ What kind of VtM material do you want to see on the Vault?<br /> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I don't have much use for most supplements so I primarily buy adventure books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T20:10:17-08:00","id":1474545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474524#post1474524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, I don't have much use for most supplements so I primarily buy adventure books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. But I wonder what the general consensus is on the stuff at the Vault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T02:06:49-08:00","id":1474555,"title":"","content":"In terms of what sells on the <i>Storyteller's Vault</i>, a rough hierarchy of what is successful would run something like the following list:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Core rulebooks (noting that you are not supposed to create an entirely standalone rulebook).</li> <li>Books about powers, and other material which can be easily imported into any chronicle.</li> <li>Generalised sourcebooks with a primary focus on supernatural society.</li> <li>Generalised sourcebooks with a primary focus upon the mortal world.</li> <li>Location sourcebooks.</li> <li>Adventures.</li> <li>Gaming aids and other similar paraphernalia.</li> </ol>That's a fairly generalised list, though; how successful a book will be is also influenced by a number of other factors. These include:<ul><li>Choice of game line; a product written for <i>Vampire</i> will normally outsell a product written for Wraith.</li> <li>Demand for the subject matter; there is clearly a lot of demand for a good Sabbat sourcebook.</li> <li>Accessibility of subject matter; a location sourcebook on Britain will sell a lot better than a location sourcebook about Syria.</li> <li>Price; consensus is that a price of $1 for every ten pages is the general market rate right now.</li> <li>Quality of product; get a decent preview up online.</li> <li>Reputation; an author how has a reputation for delivering quality may sell more books than a new author.</li> </ul><br /> So, there are a lot of factors at play. Focus on the right product and market and you can sell a large number of books, regardless of quality (though you may not get terribly positive reviews); conversely, you could write the best adventure for <i>Demon: the Fallen </i>and you would struggle to sell many copies at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T08:56:38-08:00","id":1474567,"title":"","content":"I wasn't asking for advice on what does and doesn't sell.<br /> <br /> I <i>was </i>asking what people think of the books and items now available on the Vault.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T09:17:28-08:00","id":1474568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474567#post1474567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't asking for advice on what does and doesn't sell.<br /> <br /> I <i>was </i>asking what people think of the books and items now available on the Vault.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. I love &quot;Long Hard Road Out Of Hell&quot; and generally like the Sabbat books.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T20:21:35-08:00","id":1474595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474111#post1474111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have the pure conjecture answer that the reason that Paradox Entertainment has such a mad on/hatred for the idea of playable Sabbat is a straight line dating back to the controveries of 5th Edition's release.<br /> <br /> They've had to deal with the following:<br /> <br /> * The Nazi Brujah one-line mention as a player character option getting a massive storm of controversy<br /> * The pedophile Ventrue (which wasn't even a pedophile, they just fed on children) in the sample adventure.<br /> * The entire international media shitstorm regarding the vampires in Chechnya.<br /> <br /> My assumption is that all of the bad optics from these events convinced Paradox that doing the Sabbat as player characters, you know, a group of terrorist serial killer religious fanatics <i>even when they're heroes</i> would be something that would bring down even more holy hell of controversy.<br /> <br /> This is why they have an absolutely 100% no holds barred &quot;there will never be playable Sabbat&quot; and we didn't get a Sabbat book until now: terror of controversy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have to completely agree with those conjectures, times are very different now.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T01:23:37-08:00","id":1474603,"title":"","content":"I'm a big fan of the Savage Age line, The VtM Classic Age line, Hsienfans KOTE20 books, Dion Fernandez Pinoy setting books for VtM/KotE and WtO. None of which is V5 but theres a bit of V20 in there to half answer the posed question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T01:41:16-08:00","id":1474604,"title":"","content":"Still shits me that V5 gets an entire section all of its own at the top of the front page of the Vault and everything else gets shoved into one little box that has to accomodate 9 different gamelines and 4 different editions all at once......theres some really excellent work there that gets pushed out of the public eye within hours of going up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T03:11:02-08:00","id":1474607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474604#post1474604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still shits me that V5 gets an entire section all of its own at the top of the front page of the Vault and everything else gets shoved into one little box that has to accomodate 9 different gamelines and 4 different editions all at once......theres some really excellent work there that gets pushed out of the public eye within hours of going up.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't like it, this is one shitty thing that's actually to be expected and, sincerely, their right.<br /> <br /> It belongs to Paradox and <i>their</i> current product <b><u>is</u></b> V5, like it or not. They have zero commercial interest in giving up prime space for their actual product line in favor of material for discontinued editions or V20, and no conceivable obligation of doing so.<br /> <br /> Also, lets be honest, anyone that will be interested in those materials will already be looking for them specifically anyways. A front page must be the most friendly to people that's lost on what to look for, and those people will most likely be looking for the current line and not for supplements to books published more than 20 years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T04:46:58-08:00","id":1474610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462396-storytellers-vault-is-opening-to-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition?p=1474607#post1474607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't like it, this is one shitty thing that's actually to be expected and, sincerely, their right.<br /> <br /> It belongs to Paradox and <i>their</i> current product <b><u>is</u></b> V5, like it or not. They have zero commercial interest in giving up prime space for their actual product line in favor of material for discontinued editions or V20, and no conceivable obligation of doing so.<br /> <br /> Also, lets be honest, anyone that will be interested in those materials will already be looking for them specifically anyways. A front page must be the most friendly to people that's lost on what to look for, and those people will most likely be looking for the current line and not for supplements to books published more than 20 years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All true, still annoying. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 02-14-2022, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T06:04:55-08:00","id":1474618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally pos